 The function should use a for loop to iterate over the array and compare each number to the current largest number. If a number is larger, it should be updated as the new largest number. The function should return the largest number when it is finished iterating.

Solution:
```javascript
function largestNumber(arr) {
  let largest = arr[0];
  for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > largest) {
      largest = arr[i];
    }
  }
  return largest;
}
```
